# MadGraph5 batch script: e+ e- > z > mu+ mu- at LO
#
# Why this exact process:
#   - `> z` is a diagram filter, not an on-shell requirement: of the two
#     s-channel diagrams of e+ e- > mu+ mu- only the Z's survives, so the cross
#     section is the Z term alone, with the gamma-Z interference gone. MadGraph
#     prints no gauge-invariance warning for it.
#   - At sqrt(s) = 500 GeV the filtered and unrestricted processes differ by a
#     factor of eight, so a filter that removed nothing, or the wrong diagram,
#     cannot pass for this one.
#   - iseed is the first seed of the per-seed reference
#     (gen_grammar_sigma.sh, row ee_z_only), so this run is that seed's run.
generate e+ e- > z > mu+ mu-
output ee_to_mumu_zonly -nojpeg
launch
set ebeam1 250
set ebeam2 250
set iseed 20260926
done
